    "summary": "Commemorative head of an Oba (uhunmwun elao); lost-wax cast in brass. In form of human head depicted wearing coral bead regalia: openwork  cap decorated with additional clusters of beads; single bead at front over forehead. Strands of beads at sides  and back of head. Deep coral bead collar from neck over lower lip. Has hair plaits at sides terminating in large beads. Head has three raised scarification marks above eyes; irises inlaid with iron. Central hole in top of head.",
